{"id":"u-4eceb401-14c5-4526-8312-49a9fb0644df","src":"community","title":"4 day Upper/Lower","author":"Joshua Q.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/tD2nEc-4-day-upperlower","desc":"Workouts should be doable in 45-60 mins depending on how much time you spend warming up and resting in-between sets. \n\nWarm up however much you feel you need. Keep in mind warmups can be as simple as 1 rep of 80-90% of your working weight for the exercise. \n\nRest 2-3 minutes between sets or until you feel ready.\n\nRPE means Rate of Perceived Exertion.\nTo keep it simple 10 RPE means training to failure, 9 RPE means leaving 1 rep in the tank, 8 RPE means 2 reps in the tank. \n\nIdeally you'll leave 1 rep in reserve for every set, but if you take a set to failure here and there it's not the end of the world.\n\nEvery set is in the 4-6 rep range just because that's what's optimal according to the research we have. But in reality the rep range doesn't matter too much. Any rep range will work as long you're training close to failure (2-0 reps in reserve) and aren't doing a ridiculous amount of reps like 20-30.\n\nI've added alternative exercises for you to choose from based on preference and availability.","level":["Beginner","Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":50,"joins":6,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-30T22:20:11.055Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper","Lower","Upper","Lower"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}],"note":"If you do chest supported rows instead, make sure to use a neutral grip with elbows tucked to your side to target lats"},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"T-Bar Row","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}],"note":"Any chest supported row variation works here as long as you are using a pronated grip